---
import Hero from "../components/layout/hero/Hero.astro";
import Heading from "../components/ui/Heading.astro";
import Link from "../components/ui/Link.astro";
import P from "../components/ui/P.astro";
import Main from "../layouts/Main.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";
import SocialMediaLinks from "../components/feature/social-media-links/SocialMediaLinks.astro";
import Values from "../components/feature/values/Values.astro";
import RelativeDate from "../components/ui/RelativeDate.astro";
---

<Main>
  <Hero slot="hero" />
  <div slot="content">
    <P>
      Hello 👋... I am Conrad, a human living in
      <Link href="https://www.southafrica.net/" target="_blank"
        >South Africa.
      </Link> I guess if you read this, you would like to know a little about me,
      so here it is…
    </P>
    <Heading>I have a career</Heading>
    <P>
      Professionally, I have worn many hats. I began as a Web Designer and
      dabbled in some Graphic Design. Midway into my journey, I transitioned to
      Frontend Engineering and Development. I transitioned to the role of
      Engineering Manager <RelativeDate date="'01/05/2024'" addSuffix />. I've
      also unofficially worn the hats of Product Manager, Product Designer and
      UX researcher.
    </P>
    <P>
      As a <strong>Software Engineer</strong>, I take a pragmatic approach to
      designing and building software. I always try to balance shipping the best
      we have today with an execution plan to evolve and iterate on later. I
      believe good engineering practices have always been vital, but even more
      with LLM agents around. I've been a tech lead on big initiatives and find
      great joy in being involved in projects end-to-end. I have built SaaS
      software for over <RelativeDate date="01/01/2015" />.
    </P>
    <P>
      As an <strong>Engineering Manager</strong>, I have overseen many different
      teams, and sometimes multiple teams at the same time. My outlook on
      managing is to trust by default. The engineers I manage were hired because
      they are good at their jobs. I have a bias towards trusting them and only
      address the outliers. It is important to always have fun. Play games
      (GeoGuessr, Gartic Phone, take your pick), get the team invested in the
      same goals and celebrate together.
    </P>
    <Heading>My core values</Heading>
    <P
      >I created my own, personal, set of Core Values in which I function every
      day. I periodically revisit these values, making sure I still adhere to
      them and that they are still relevant.
    </P>
    <Values />
    <Heading>I have a personal life too, you know</Heading>
    <P
      >I am a successful family man who loves his wife of
      <RelativeDate date="04/13/2013" /> and has 4 beautiful children. I don't claim
      to be perfect and am constantly growing as a person. But I enjoy life, am kind
      where I can be and ask myself the hard questions when I find it difficult. I
      believe in the power of reflection and soul searching.
    </P>
    <P>
      Also, I love swimming. Which is what inspired the design of this website
      🏊🏻.
    </P>
    <Heading>More</Heading>
    <P> You can find me in some other places of the internet too: </P>
    <SocialMediaLinks class="flex flex-col gap-2" />
  </div>
</Main>
